{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:51:29Z","created_by_operation":"op_6984be3f4f0e4bc2ae056661d8b32972","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_a064ad78d4e9c3be24b97956392ef696a38d8730b5120f2c65f0a97519f8795e","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"foundationagents/metagpt@11cdf466d042 snapshot 32a1dc0084829e9e","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_0817de0dd1b696eb439dd4c2638a6229f968c75799d3fe6a40feddf5817d4102","slc_730d515e8eb6148b8f17fb8033d3145e8088bc5e2b53d14b62cf1194127a3336","slc_ad544efe177125518206919cd7bab1bb8f99bd8bf2f3784e336259a5958c691d","slc_fb76097f9769e1d3c5c56cb028a64a5da003149e4bb92759deb2770b2d52893f"],"source_ids":["src_de73073561d453b4aaa21d8d677387a3"],"text":"Configuration is initialized with `metagpt --init-config`, creating ~/.metagpt/config2.yaml which users edit; the example config supports api_type values like openai, azure, ollama, and groq with model, base_url, and api_key fields.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:51:29Z","updated_by_operation":"op_6984be3f4f0e4bc2ae056661d8b32972"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:51:29Z","created_by_operation":"op_6984be3f4f0e4bc2ae056661d8b32972","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_ab15aab1a20e5dcd259cc6632555f753b00a4986a5bfbb32e8518c12b3b71e87","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=specifications","setting":"foundationagents/metagpt@11cdf466d042 snapshot 32a1dc0084829e9e","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_908e4f9c5fa2e2d1531c095b5e62848a9038b4c61df9f7d466c10daafa720f22"],"source_ids":["src_de73073561d453b4aaa21d8d677387a3"],"text":"MetaGPT takes a one-line requirement as input and outputs artifacts such as user stories, competitive analysis, requirements, data structures, APIs, and documents.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:51:29Z","updated_by_operation":"op_6984be3f4f0e4bc2ae056661d8b32972"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:51:29Z","created_by_operation":"op_6984be3f4f0e4bc2ae056661d8b32972","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_cd843948ea7ceb4160ab60df2728d0dd571866c25d1973d08b0811a7719b102c","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"foundationagents/metagpt@11cdf466d042 snapshot 32a1dc0084829e9e","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_04ee06cca527a63acbbd8f4e52eeb79f7cffbf0e23068162023194c2a6c1c223","slc_4e2bf239debe2fcd67dea6b6a6c8e1a27d2a7e322380ee82cde6bf061aba9b20","slc_50e2f1fc0d5764617d06daf7f6f1dd8f1523036e6f56d6e636a935bacd5c510e"],"source_ids":["src_de73073561d453b4aaa21d8d677387a3"],"text":"MetaGPT can also be used as a Python library via `metagpt.software_company.generate_repo`, which returns a ProjectRepo whose structure can be printed.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:51:29Z","updated_by_operation":"op_6984be3f4f0e4bc2ae056661d8b32972"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:51:29Z","created_by_operation":"op_6984be3f4f0e4bc2ae056661d8b32972","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_cf7a281f5f1048638a9e09ddbfdeb3c9e6af2d3bb23a8ca96f1db8ef5432c36c","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=relevance","setting":"foundationagents/metagpt@11cdf466d042 snapshot 32a1dc0084829e9e","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_1aaa168c693b09e8f71b1671432ae03b21110d34c028e44e79ad185f2829ea81","slc_3279bbe4f337ed4070957cfa42b8c09775dcff8e1988aacdffed4fa63f4f7649","slc_d1883ea61025a48b49dff3607ccf25bdc2927555d818be5ea2e6da4b2dab418a","slc_ead2de40c1ea48a9a679bfcfc5971d9ac9794f9e573e768dcb2cb2f07684fa6a","slc_f326981fadae5b2d7f1b3fc893d3eb74261b6f90778796449efef4afb8fd557d"],"source_ids":["src_422f5425d4d259f7af5caf66649071a7","src_de73073561d453b4aaa21d8d677387a3","src_fedc9ba74ed75a85994d87da9498ad60"],"text":"The project is MIT-licensed, open-sourced June 2023, and its ICLR 2024 paper on multi-agent collaborative meta programming is cited alongside related work such as AFlow, SPO, AOT, FACT, and SELA.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:51:29Z","updated_by_operation":"op_6984be3f4f0e4bc2ae056661d8b32972"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:51:29Z","created_by_operation":"op_6984be3f4f0e4bc2ae056661d8b32972","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_dd704caf7d906bc1ffa041557c9430b2f1386eeb70ac695f53c47a609aa35ed4","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=limitations","setting":"foundationagents/metagpt@11cdf466d042 snapshot 32a1dc0084829e9e","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_b8dae53f79d780bfbeb6ee3fbf49de9265ee18db7bca03a66e54c32a0aca469f"],"source_ids":["src_5d2d9a71369c5bde97cdbd9bd14505e9"],"text":"Per the FAQ, incremental/differential updates (--inc with project path or name), multiple programming languages, and multiple natural languages are supported only in experimental versions.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:51:29Z","updated_by_operation":"op_6984be3f4f0e4bc2ae056661d8b32972"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:51:29Z","created_by_operation":"op_6984be3f4f0e4bc2ae056661d8b32972","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_e0d51138e9165e81452f9a7dbc0964e6fa601bb1b272c45eca158b60eb7bc63d","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=limitations","setting":"foundationagents/metagpt@11cdf466d042 snapshot 32a1dc0084829e9e","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_b8dae53f79d780bfbeb6ee3fbf49de9265ee18db7bca03a66e54c32a0aca469f"],"source_ids":["src_5d2d9a71369c5bde97cdbd9bd14505e9"],"text":"The FAQ states no quantitative success-rate analysis has been done, though gpt-4-turbo code generation reportedly succeeds significantly more often than gpt-3.5-turbo, and loading existing large projects is described as very difficult.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:51:29Z","updated_by_operation":"op_6984be3f4f0e4bc2ae056661d8b32972"}
